design_notes:
Proposal overview: implement a small handshake layer around the SDK's stream producer that tracks a three-state lifecycle per-request: OPEN -> DRAINING -> CLOSED. The consumer surface (async iterator or ReadableStream) owns an AbortSignal; when the consumer requests early-return, the adapter transitions to DRAINING and notifies the runtime. The runtime will finish emitting any buffered completion tokens (configurable limit via options.drainTimeoutMs) then transition to CLOSED. If immediateAbort=true, the adapter cancels the transport immediately.

Key trade-offs considered:
- Strict immediate abort minimizes cost but can lose final tokens. We default to draining to preserve user intent for completions.
- Draining adds complexity and possible latency on shutdown; mitigated by drainTimeoutMs and a telemetry counter for truncated drains.

Implementation sketch (pseudo):
- toWebStream(asyncIterable, { signal, immediateAbort = false, drainTimeoutMs = 250 } ) => ReadableStream {
  - pull: ensure we call asyncIter.next(); write chunk; if asyncIter done -> close;
  - cancel(reason): if immediateAbort -> cancel transport; else set DRAINING and notify producer, start drain timer; after drainTimer expires, force cancel.
}
- toAsyncIterator(readable, { signal, immediateAbort=false }) => AsyncIterator {
  - uses reader.read() -> yields values
  - return(): call reader.cancel(reason) and follow same handshake rules
}

api_examples:
// Convert SDK stream to Web Stream and attach SIGTERM handler
const rs = client.streamCompletion({ prompt: '...' }).toWebStream({ signal: controller.signal });
process.on('SIGTERM', async () => {
  // graceful: let in-flight token buffer drain for up to 300ms
  controller.abort(new Error('SIGTERM'));
});

// Convert ReadableStream to async iterator and early-return gracefully
const iter = toAsyncIterator(myReadable, { immediateAbort: false });
for await (const chunk of iter) {
  if (chunk.text.includes('[STOP]')) {
    // consumer chooses to stop but wants the final buffer flushed before close
    await iter.return();
    break;
  }
}

// Opt-in immediate abort (low-latency, lose last tokens)
const fastIter = toAsyncIterator(stream, { immediateAbort: true });
await fastIter.return(); // triggers immediate transport cancel
